  "outcomes": [
    "Creation and lost-response retry produce one pending invitation with a hashed secret",
    "Malformed tokens, anonymous/missing actors, unverified profiles and token takeover are rejected",
    "Read-only preview exposes only inviter presentation; self response, non-owner revoke and raw table access are denied",
    "Acceptance creates one mutual connection, consumes the link and safely replays only the same decision/recipient",
    "Either participant can remove; unrelated removal and old acceptance replay cannot restore membership or alter existing grants",
    "A genuinely new invitation reconnects without duplicates; the other participant can remove too",
    "Revoked requests stay revoked across creation retry; a declined single-use invitation cannot create a friendship",
    "Bounded owner-only invitation pages contain no bearer token or token hash",
    "Two native sessions waiting on one invitation yield exactly one accepted recipient",
    "Revocation committed while acceptance waits prevents acceptance and preserves real independent grants",
    "Concurrent same-recipient retries agree; revocation after committed acceptance leaves the friendship intact",
    "A real transaction failure rolls back invitation consumption and allows successful recovery",
    "Concurrent creation respects the 20-pending-request bound; revocation releases capacity without restoring old tokens",
    "Deleting a related profile cascades its private invitation/membership rows and leaves unrelated profiles/grants intact"
  ],
  "limitations": "Selected native SQL contracts. Auth users/uid and verified-profile column are explicit prerequisites; no hosted JWT/Auth, PostgREST, full migration chain, pending-request delivery, Angular route or UI parity is certified."
